 "findings": {
  "good": [],
  "more": [
   {
    "condition": "N4",
    "good_when": "two developers who each build the billing part for an issuer whose terms are, say, 20\u65e5\u7de0\u3081\u7fcc\u670810\u65e5\u6255\u3044 put the same rows in each invoice and print the same issue date and payment deadline, because the principles say how the closing period and the deadline follow from the issuer's terms, and each principle item holds a single decision. Today P2.1, P2.3, and P3.6 each bundle two decisions, and nothing says how the closing period comes from the free-text answer to \u7de0\u3081\u65e5\u3068\u652f\u6255\u6761\u4ef6."
   },
   {
    "condition": "N9",
    "good_when": "the developer who builds the command finds one order for a first run: the S1 and S3 sequences agree on whether the statement is checked before or after the issuer is asked their questions, so a first-time user with a faulty statement isn't made to answer every question and only then told to fix the file. The components figure also agrees with the sequences on what the issuer-info store and the printing part hand back: the issuer info, and the number of sheets sent."
   },
   {
    "condition": "N13",
    "good_when": "a developer who designs the billing, numbering, and command parts and their tests from the document alone finds no open question: they know how the closing period and payment deadline come from the issuer's terms, which comes first on a first run (the statement check or the issuer's questions), and that a run stopped in the middle of the questions leaves nothing saved, which the S3 sequence shows."
   },
   {
    "condition": "N15",
    "good_when": "a developer who adds a file or folder knows where it belongs and why, because the directory structure gives its own strategies, each tagged and with its intent, like the other views do. The view decisions that are made today without a stated strategy also each come with their reason, so a developer who changes them knows what the change would break: putting numbering in its own part, and checking the statement before printing in S1."
   }
  ]
 },
